# Keychron Q6 Max (3434:0861) and M6 8K (3434:d049) — raw HID access so that
# launcher.keychron.com can see them in Brave.
#
# Without this every /dev/hidraw* is crw------- root:root, the browser runs as
# ulu and cannot open any of them. WebHID does not report that as an error: the
# device picker simply comes up EMPTY, which reads as "nothing happens at all".
# That is exactly how this was found.
#
# uaccess, not a group: systemd-logind puts an ACL on the node for whoever holds
# the active local session, so access ends with the logout instead of living on
# in a group membership. It needs a local seat — fine here, ulu is on seat0.
#
# Matched by VENDOR, not by product: a third Keychron device should not need a
# rule change. Both devices are used WIRED here without exception (ulu, session
# 5) — over the 2.4 GHz dongle the keyboard may enumerate under a different id
# and would need its own line, and over Bluetooth the launcher cannot reach it
# at all.
SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{idVendor}=="3434", TAG+="uaccess"
